<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Tangents: equation of the tangent at a given point (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find the equation of the tangent to the curve</p>
\[ f(x) = {@fx@} \]
<p>at the point where \( x = {@aa@} \). Work in three steps.</p>
<p><strong>Step 1.</strong> The gradient of the tangent, \( m = f'({@aa@}) \):</p>
<div>\( m = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>Step 2.</strong> The \( y \)-coordinate of the point of tangency, \( f({@aa@}) \):</p>
<div>\( f({@aa@}) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p><strong>Step 3.</strong> The equation of the tangent, in the form \( y = mx + c \):</p>
<div>\( y = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: the gradient.</strong> \( f'(x) = {@dfx@} \), so</p>
\[ m = f'({@aa@}) = {@mt@}. \]
<p><strong>Step 2: the point.</strong> \( f({@aa@}) = {@fa@} \), so the tangent touches the curve at \( ({@aa@},\ {@fa@}) \).</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: the line.</strong> Use \( y = f'(a)(x-a) + f(a) \):</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
y &= {@mt@}\left(x - ({@aa@})\right) + ({@fa@}) \\
  &= {@tl@}.
\end{align*}
\]
<p>Check: at \( x = {@aa@} \) the tangent gives \( y = {@subst(aa, x, tl)@} \), the same height as the curve, and its gradient \( {@mt@} \) matches \( f'({@aa@}) \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[/* f(x) = c3 x^3 + c2 x^2 + c1 x + c0 (a quadratic when c3 = 0), point x = aa.
   Filters keep the numbers small and make every common error give a different line. */
cands : sublist(
  create_list([u3, u2, u1, u0, u], u3, [0, 1, -1], u2, -3, 3, u1, -4, 4, u0, -5, 5, u, [-2, -1, 1, 2, 3]),
  lambda([z], block([m, fv],
    m  : 3*z[1]*z[5]^2 + 2*z[2]*z[5] + z[3],
    fv : z[1]*z[5]^3 + z[2]*z[5]^2 + z[3]*z[5] + z[4],
    is((z[1] # 0 or z[2] # 0) and m # 0 and fv # 0 and m # fv and abs(m) <= 20 and abs(fv) <= 20
       and fv # -2*m*z[5] and fv # -m*z[5]))));
pick : rand(cands);
fx  : pick[1]*x^3 + pick[2]*x^2 + pick[3]*x + pick[4];
aa  : pick[5];
dfx : diff(fx, x);
mt  : subst(aa, x, dfx);              /* gradient of the tangent */
fa  : subst(aa, x, fx);               /* height of the point of tangency */
tl  : expand(mt*(x - aa) + fa);       /* model tangent */
w_noshift : expand(mt*(x - aa));      /* forgot + f(a) */
w_sign    : expand(mt*(x + aa) + fa); /* used (x + a) */
w_noa     : mt*x + fa;                /* used y = m x + f(a) */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
